{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>By the plague, before YHWH.</b> By that which was fitting for them — measure for measure. They sinned with the tongue, and their tongues stretched out to their navels, and worms emerged from their tongues and entered into their navels; therefore it says 'by the plague,' and this is 'before YHWH' — by that measure appropriate to them according to the attributes of the Holy One, blessed be He, who measures measure for measure. So explained Rashi, of blessed memory."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:31.801422628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}